*---------------------------------------------------------------
* mm.lseg.equ -- the play-only LOW SEGMENT (docs/LOOP-S1.md,
* ruling 2026-10-10): main RAM $1300-$1FFF, loaded at boot from
* the boot volume's LSEG file by KSEG_LOAD. Code and cells fill
* the first pages; the caches sit above them and are NOT in the
* file. The image file's io_buffer is NOT here: it is one of the
* kernel pool's eight (PRC_ALLC_IBF): the pool IS ProDOS's
* eight-FCB ceiling and a ninth open file made the kernel's own
* spawns fail ("command not found" at the seventh held file,
* measured) -- see docs/LOOP-S1-NOTES.md sec 9. Layout is pinned
* by scripts/check_lseg.py.
*---------------------------------------------------------------
LSEG_ORG    equ   $1300
LSEG_MAXPG  equ   8             ;code + cells, $1300-$1AFF
LP_MAST     equ   $1B00         ;master index, 128 lo + 128 hi
LP_IDX0     equ   $1C00         ;index block 0, pinned (2 pages)
LP_SLOT     equ   $1E00         ;one more index block (2 pages)
LSEG_TOP    equ   $2000         ;first byte above the region

*-- refusals (kernel codes, clear of the MLI's $01-$5F and the
*-- kernel's own $E0-$F1; mount maps each to its message)
LPE_SPARSE  equ   $D1           ;a zero pointer below EOF
LPE_2MG     equ   $D2           ;a 2IMG container
LPE_NOTTREE equ   $D3           ;not a tree file
LPE_NOROOM  equ   $D4           ;DEVLST is full
LPE_PRODOS  equ   $D6           ;not the ProDOS 2.4 pinned cells
LPE_NOSAVED equ   $D7           ;bye left no loop to re-attach

*-- ProDOS 2.4 MLI cells (docs/LOOP-S2-NOTES.md sec 2), LC
*-- common
*-- bmaStat: bit 7 = bitmap needs writing
BMA_STAT    equ   $FE99
BMA_DEV     equ   $FE9A         ;bmaDev: the unit that owns it
*-- UpdateBitMap (CLC LDA BMA_STAT ...)
BMA_PIN     equ   $EB42
